// ADR 0071 M1.4c / filed-defect register D17: the SECRET half of the container element
// widths. This is the fixture that catches the one wrong mirror every public element is
// blind to — copying the CHANNEL arms verbatim.
//
// The channel encode tests the value argument's raw TYPE HANDLE against the scalar codes
// {i64,i32,u8,bool}. That works for a channel because its element map rejects `secret`
// outright. A container's does not: `Shared<secret u8>` is constructible. A `secret u8`
// element is an INTERNED HANDLE, not a scalar code, so it matches no arm and falls to
// whatever the final `else` does — silently the wrong encoding. The mirror therefore
// strips the qualifier FIRST and chooses the width from the inner type, exactly as the
// oracle's `unsecret()` does.
//
// ⚠ The existing `c71_secret_shared` cannot catch this: its element is `secret i64`,
// which strips to width 64, so the encode is a no-op either way. It takes a NARROW
// secret to make the bug observable.
//
// A secret element needs nothing beyond the public path — the oracle's secret output is
// instruction-for-instruction its public output, differing only in the constructor
// symbol (`sentinel_shared_new_secret`), which is orthogonal to width and which scg
// already picked correctly. The width conversion is `zext`, never `sext`, so the unused
// high bits of a secret cell are deterministically ZERO — no residue, no value-dependent
// bit pattern. `zext`/`trunc` are single fixed-latency integer instructions: no branch,
// no table, no divide, so no new taint sink. The strip is a CODEGEN width decision made
// long after `secret_leak` has run — the `Type` stays `Secret(..)` on both sides and
// every read below still type-checks as `secret`, which is D6's named invariant.
//
// Trace: 7 (secret u8) + 5 (secret bool, true) + 30 (secret i32 through a lock) = 42,
// declassified once each for the public exit code. Exit 42, no stdout.

fn main() -> i64 {
    let x: secret u8 = 7 as u8;
    let s: Shared<secret u8> = shared_new(x);
    let r: secret u8 = shared_get(s);

    let b: secret bool = true;
    let sb: Shared<secret bool> = shared_new(b);
    let rb: secret bool = shared_get(sb);

    let i: secret i32 = 30 as i32;
    let m: Mutex<secret i32> = mutex_new(i);
    let g = lock(m);
    let gv: secret i32 = *g;

    (declassify(r) as i64)
        + (if declassify(rb) { 5 } else { 0 })
        + (declassify(gv) as i64)
}
